WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.069
-Welcome, everybody!
Please.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.103
-Happy --
-Love you, Jimmy!

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.372
-I love you.
Happy Thri-day!

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.040
-Thri-day, I love it.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.209
-[ As Rebecca Black ]
♪ Thri-day ♪

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.276
-I didn't make that up, right?
Is that a thing?

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.645
-It is now.
-Happy Thri-day?

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.948
-It's Thursday.
-Yeah, but I'm -- Thri-day.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.683
[ Laughter ]
'Cause the energy --

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.950
I'm already
in the weekend already.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.754
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.190
-Well, guys,
this Sunday is Father's Day.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.258
That's right. So --

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:30.563
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.797
So make sure you call your dad,

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.633
even though
you'd both prefer a text.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.368
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.269
But talking with Dad
on Father's Day is fun.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:39.004
It's a great way to catch up
on which neighbors

00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:40.240
are annoying him
for which reasons.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:44.543
"This guy parks his car in front
of his house all the time.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.845
[ Laughter ]
This guy, he plays his music --"

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:48.481
"Okay, good, Dad."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.815
That's right,
Father's Day is this Sunday,

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:53.653
and Americans are expected
to spend over $20 billion.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.887
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.289
That story, again --
on Sunday, over 20 billion

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:58.858
scratch-off tickets
will be sold.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.260
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.762
"Good luck, Dad."

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.731
Let's get to some news.
After his week-long trip

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.832
to Europe, President Biden
is finally back

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.768
in Washington, D.C.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.404
When he saw his schedule filled
with meetings on infrastructure,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.840
immigration, and inflation,
his first thought was,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.009
"I already miss Putin."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.078
Yep, returning home
was pretty emotional for Biden,

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.646
mostly 'cause
on the flight there,

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.749
he realized that he
"Home Aloned" Pete Buttigieg.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.016
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:27.019
"Pete!"

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.422
"Keep the change,
you filthy animal!"

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.790
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.026
But this is big.
Today, Biden signed

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.128
the Juneteenth National
Independence Day Act...

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.229
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.465
...making Juneteenth
a federal holiday!

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:47.006
[ Applause ]

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:50.176
The bill hit Biden's desk after
it was passed in Congress,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.312
but 14 members of the House
voted against it.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:54.580
[ Audience booing ]

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.582
Can we --
Can we see who they were?

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:57.883
Yeah.
-Oh.

00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.485
-That's -- That's about right.
That's about right.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.754
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.523
That looks like the white-paint
sample section at Home Depot.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.192
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.961
"What do you think, honey?

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.430
Should we paint the bathroom
Mike Rogers or Thomas Massie?"

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.598
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:16.569
And I saw this -- Jared Kushner
just signed a book deal.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.404
Yep, his book will come out
next year.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.373
But he already
has a few titles in mind.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.375
Check these out.
First --

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.211
-Ah, here we go.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.613
-What's up, dude?
-Let me guess.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:30.082
Well, you're gonna make fun
of Jared Kushner, right?

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:33.018
By saying a bunch
of fake book titles.

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:35.454
-I mean...yeah,
that was the plan.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:39.325
-And, of course, each title
will pop up as a graphic,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.195
so everyone can see it
and "laugh" about it.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.395
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:44.830
-Right.
That's kind of what I do.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.633
It's the whole first
10 minutes of the show.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.968
-I -- I know exactly
how this will go down.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.870
Okay, the top of the screen
will have, like, a weird picture

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.973
of Kushner, and it'll say,
"Kushner's Book Titles."

00:02:54.973 --> 00:02:58.043
And then, under that,
you'll list fake titles, like,

00:02:58.043 --> 00:03:01.047
"50 Shades of White."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.716
Or -- Or
"Diary of a Wimpy Adult."

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:04.951
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.019
Or "Are You There, Don?

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.855
It's Me, Your Creepy
Son-in-Law."

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.389
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:11.623
And then you'll do,

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:13.526
"Eat, Pray, Ask Daddy
for a Million Dollars."

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.794
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.664
Oh, or -- or "Gone With the
Slightest Gust of Wind."

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.964
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.799
And then you'll finish it off
with something like,

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:25.237
"The Sun Also Rises (While I
Sleep Standing Up in a Coffin)."

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:26.905
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:29.842
I'm guessing
that's how this is gonna go.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.443
-Yeah.

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.346
You nailed it.
-Well, that's a fun bit.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.314
You should do it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:36.449
-All right.
We'll do it tomorrow.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.918
Perfect.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.686
Well, guys, get this.
I read that for next year's

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:45.558
